# Served by Cloudflare's static-asset router, which reads this file from dist/.
#
# /install.sh is the one-line installer for the command line:
#
#   curl -fsSL https://gitwarren.com/install.sh | sh
#
# The script itself lives in the app repository as packaging/install.sh, next
# to the tarball it installs and the CLI whose `service install` it runs, so
# it is versioned with them and this site stays free of app code. A 302 so
# curl -L follows it; the body a visitor gets is always whatever is on main.
/install.sh https://raw.githubusercontent.com/klarluft/gitwarren-app/main/packaging/install.sh 302
